WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.313 --> 00:00:04.375
- Gonna ride till the
wheels come off, baby.

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:07.794
- [Manny] Lowrider bicycles
is a special everything.

00:00:07.794 --> 00:00:11.439
Special frame, special
wheels, special paint.

00:00:11.439 --> 00:00:13.348
Everything is special.

00:00:13.348 --> 00:00:16.459
The bicycles we make, is made with love

00:00:16.459 --> 00:00:18.792
because it's with our hands.

00:00:22.123 --> 00:00:23.587
(funky music)

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:24.420
- [Voiceover] You know those bikes Snoop

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.567
and countless other
rappers rode around in,

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.753
you know the ones that
ooze that West Coast style?

00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:31.061
Lowrider bikes.

00:00:31.061 --> 00:00:33.809
Low to the ground,
chromed out, gold-plated.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:36.232
They're an extension of
lowrider car culture.

00:00:36.232 --> 00:00:38.093
And they all started here.

00:00:38.093 --> 00:00:41.926
- I am the godfather of
the lowrider bicycles.

00:00:44.193 --> 00:00:45.695
When I was 10 years old,

00:00:45.695 --> 00:00:48.391
I used to fix all the
bicycles in the neighborhood.

00:00:48.391 --> 00:00:51.363
I always dreamed with
a motorcycle and a car,

00:00:51.363 --> 00:00:54.350
but since I was too small and no money,

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.933
so I put my mind into bicycles.

00:00:58.911 --> 00:01:01.098
- [Voiceover] A mainstay in
Compton and West Coast culture,

00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:05.265
these iconic bikes were actually
first created in Mexico.

00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:11.004
- [Voiceover] I brought
the lowrider to California

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.087
in early 80's.

00:01:13.194 --> 00:01:14.487
- [Voiceover] And soon after,

00:01:14.487 --> 00:01:17.155
locals took notice of
the shiny, swaggy rides

00:01:17.155 --> 00:01:19.445
hanging in his shop.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:23.052
- When I start making
bicycles in this place

00:01:23.052 --> 00:01:27.639
people come and they say hey, can
you make me one of those?

00:01:27.639 --> 00:01:29.076
And then they spread,

00:01:29.076 --> 00:01:33.956
and now we have customers
from all over the world.

00:01:33.956 --> 00:01:35.988
- This is one of Manny's
creations right here.

00:01:35.988 --> 00:01:40.388
He's almost a pack-rat,
he put everything on here.

00:01:40.388 --> 00:01:44.925
He blew my mind when he
put it on there for me.

00:01:44.925 --> 00:01:46.953
- [Manny] It's completely different

00:01:46.953 --> 00:01:48.175
than the regular bike,

00:01:48.175 --> 00:01:52.342
in the way they look, in the
way they drive, it's a art.

00:01:54.524 --> 00:01:58.843
People dream, and we
make the dream come true.

00:01:58.843 --> 00:02:01.343
(funky music)

